  "scope": "Selected durable-record cleanup: original effect-byte conversion, completed-group plan/state/size/delete checks, and stale local-token projection. Native owners retain raw SQL, eager row collection, foreign-key cascades and transaction ownership.",
  "limitations": [
    "Frozen lower-helper bodies come from 63df912e and were unchanged by the preceding uncommitted sequence-gate and compaction-batch slices. They share native storage and existing codecs/admission, but not migrated cleanup policy.",
    "The 192 group-deletion comparisons cover four source forms, three lifecycle stages and sixteen storage/trigger variants. They compare exact errors/results and in-transaction mutation prefixes, then roll back and verify every original table. Corrupt fixtures are not supported recovery checkpoints.",
    "The 288 effect-size and 96 stale-cache comparisons cover four source forms, three lifecycle stages and eight low-level variants. Original local order, duplicates, opaque tokens and unchecked local payloads are retained. Neither operation writes, repairs or changes transaction state.",
    "Nine direct adapter tests exercise read/plan/completeness/size/delete ordering, negative and saturating byte counts, deletion cardinality, unchanged native fault ownership, unwinds without retry or compensation, and empty-local native reads.",
    "The borrowed-transaction test observes the caller's uncommitted membership change, then demonstrates that a late branch-delete refusal leaves the original deletion prefix inside the still-active outer transaction. Only the caller's rollback restores it.",
    "The previous full-batch frozen implementation now calls independently frozen effect-size/group-delete/reconciliation helpers. Complete related-crate tests rerun the batch-level rollback, public late-failure cache protection, peer reconciliation and restart paths through the migrated implementation.",
    "No receipt decoding, token normalization, complete-graph revalidation, recovery admission, nested transaction, watermark repair, commit, rollback or retry is added by this adapter. Native SQL constraints, query diagnostics and full-batch commit ownership remain unchanged.",
    "No new Linux, remote CI, live GUI, actual exported-source execution, complete independent durable recovery, power-loss, disk-full, multi-host race or performance evidence is claimed."
  ],
